* @title Trace every function call with &FTRACE
* @match substring/i
* @expect >>>
* LEVEL 0 RETURN OF DBL = 42
* <<<
* Setting &FTRACE turns on call/return tracing for all defined functions at
* once, without naming each with TRACE. It is the blunt-instrument companion to
* TRACE(...,'FUNCTION'): handy when you do not yet know which function is
* misbehaving. The output format is the same call/return ladder.
        DEFINE('DBL(X)')              :(MAIN)
DBL     DBL = X + X                   :(RETURN)
MAIN    &FTRACE = 10
        OUTPUT = DBL(21)
END
